 ## Overview
-Palette Texture Volume Rendering accelerates 2D slicing volume visualization on mobile devices by combining adaptive screen-resolution rendering, compressed palette textures, and basic graphics hardware functionality [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of slow interactive rendering on low-end hardware by embedding the transfer function directly into a compressed 8-bit indexed texture format, avoiding explicit CPU-side transfer function application [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from siblings by prioritizing memory efficiency and fast texture updates through compression, accepting lower visual fidelity (blurred boundaries after upscaling) in exchange for interactivity on constrained devices like PDAs [S1, unofficial].
